$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Preparation of 4-(p-nitrophenoxy)biphenyl-
(II) A prebaked two-neck round bottom flask equipped with condenser and
magnetic stirrer bar was charged with 59 mmol of 1-chloro-4-nitrobenzene
(9.29 g) in excess of DMF (180 ml). Subsequently, 59mmol of biphenyl-4-ol
(10 g) and anhydrous K2CO3 (8.15 g) were added to the solution and the
mixture was refluxed for a day at 120 °C under inert (N2) atmosphere.
After 24 h, the reaction was stopped and the mixture was allowed to cool
down to room temperature. The mixture was then poured into 600 ml of
distilled water to yield dark yellow precipitates of (II). The solid was
collected by filtration and repeatedly washed with distilled water.
Finally, the product was recrystallized with toluene. The crystalline
structure of (II) was confirmed by X-ray crystallographic analysis and it
was reported elsewhere [20]. 4, 4'-bis(p-nitrophenoxy)biphenyl - (IV),
yield 83%. Preparation of 4, 4'-bis(p-nitrophenoxy)biphenyl - (IV) To
synthesize (IV), the aforementioned procedure used for the preparation of
(II) was employed, except the use of 10 g (54 mmol) of
4,4'-dihydroxybiphenyl instead of biphenyl-4-ol. The amounts of other
reactants were also adjusted stoichiometrically. The crystal structure of
(IV) was reported earlier [21]. decomposition temperature >210 °C,
molecular weight: 428.4 gmol-1. Elemental analysis (% CHN) calc. for
C24H16N2O6: C, 67.29; H, 3.76; N, 6.54; and found C, 67.58; H, 3.66; N,
6.37. FTIR (KBr, thin film, cm-1): 1590 (Ar.C=C), 1505 and 1367 (N-O),
1171 (C-OC). 1H NMR (300 MHz, DMSO-d6, δ ppm): 8.27 (d, J=8.2 Hz, 4H),
7.21 (d, J=6.8 Hz, 4H), 7.39 (d, J=6.9 Hz, 4H), 7.63 (d, J=7.2 Hz, 4H).
