$DATUM To a suspension of bis(3-isopropyl-4-methoxyphenyl)iodonium
tetrafluoroborate23 (9.5 g) (9) and copper bronze (1.6 g) in
dichloromethane (40 mL) was added a solution of methyl
(3,5-dibromo-4-hydroxyphenyl)acetate (5 g) (8a) and triethylamine (1.4 g)
in dichloromethane (25 mL) dropwise at room temperature. The mixture was
stirred overnight and then filtered through Celite. Purification on a
column (silica gel) and recrystallization from methanol gave 7.3 g (83%)
of methyl [3,5-dibromo-4-(4-methoxy-3-isopropylphenoxy) phenyl] acetate
(10a): methyl [3,5-dibromo-4-(4-methoxy-3-isopropylphenoxy) phenyl]
acetate (10a), yield 7.3 g (83%) 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 1.18 (d, 6H, J = 6.9
Hz), 3.28 (m, 1H), 3.59 (s, 2H), 3.73 (s, 3H), 3.76 (s, 3H), 6.40 (dd,
1H, J = 8.7 Hz, J = 3.2 Hz), 6.68 (d, 1H, J = 8.9 Hz), 6.85 (d, 1H, J =
3.2 Hz), 7.52 (s, 2H); 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ 22.6, 27.1, 39.7, 52.5, 55.8,
110.8, 111.5, 114.3, 118.9, 133.4, 133.9, 138.8, 148.9, 150.7, 152.3,
170.9; LC-MS (ES-1), m/z 471 (M); LC-MS (ES + 1), m/z 473 (M).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
