$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of 4-(4’’-tert-butylphenyloxy)-4’-(4”’-methoxyphenyloxy)
benzophenone (20) A round bottom flask was charged with a 2 g (6.20 mmol)
sample of 4, 1.13 g (7.50 mmol) of 4-tert-butylphenol, 1.55 g (11.2 mmol)
of potassium carbonate. To this mixture was added 8.6 mL of DMAc and the
resulting solution was heated to 180 °C over the course of 4 hours under
a nitrogen atmosphere. The reaction mixture was diluted with
dichloromethane and washed with saturate NaOH and NaCl water for three
times to remove DMAc, potassium carbonate and excess 4-tert-butylphenol.
The organic layer was dried over MgSO4, filtered, evaporated. The white
solid was recrystallized from the mixture of n-hexane/chloroform (4:1)
gave white solid and dried in vacuo at 40 °C for 3 hours (2.31 g, 5.1
mmol, 83%). IR (KBr): 3059, 2996, 1644, 1596, 1500, 1312, 1235, 1161,
1150, 1113, 1105, 1036, 876, 836 cm-1. 1H NMR (CDCl3, r.t.): δ 7.76 (d, J
= 8.8 Hz, 2H), 7.75 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 2H), 7.33 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 2H),
7.04-6.89 (m, 10H), 3.81 (s, 3H), 1.32 (s, 9H) ppm; 13C NMR (CDCl3,
r.t.): δ 194.3, 162.3, 161.6, 156.6, 153.0, 148.6, 147.4, 132.2, 132.1,
132.0, 131.7, 126.8, 121.6, 119.6, 116.9, 116.2, 115.0, 55.6, 34.4, 31.4
ppm.
