$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 3.3 1-amino-2-(2''-methyl-4''-propionitrile)phenoxy-4-hydroxy
anthraquinone (6) 15.9 g (0.05 mol) compound 1, 19.4 g (0.12 mol)
compound 5, 60 mL chlorobenzene and 11.2 g (0.2 mol) potassium hydroxide
were added into 250 mL three-necked flask, heated and refluxed with
stirring. The reaction mixture was traced by TLC to reactant spot
disappeared and cooled to room temperature. The reaction mixture was
diluted with anhydrous methanol to compound 6 separated out. The reaction
mixture was filtered, the filter cake was washed with anhydrous methanol
and cold water and dried to give the crude product 6 as a red solid.
(18.1 g, 45.5 mmol). The crude product was purified by column
chromatography eluted with cyclohexane : acetone (V:V = 4:1) to give the
desired product. 1-amino-2-(2'-methyl-4'-propionitrile)phenoxy-4-hydroxy
anthraquinone (6), 83.7%, red solid m.p. 230-231℃; C24H18N2O4,
calculating value: C, 72.35; H, 4.55; N, 7.03. measured value: C, 72.33;
H, 4.54; N, 6.99. δH (CDCl3): 2.18 (3H, s), 2.67(2H, t), 2.95(2H, t),
6.21-8.39(8H, m). m/z(%): 398(M+, 29.169), 358(25.891), 344(2.494),
254(2.326), 238(2.326).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of
1-amino-2-[2-methyl-4-(methoxycarbonylethyl)phenoxy]-4-hydroxyanthraquinone
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Hu, Ying-Yu; Li, Hong-Bin; Sun, Ling; Shen, Yong-jia
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Youji Huaxue (2000), 20(4), 533-536

$RFMT $RIREG SCHEME82 STEP1
