$DATUM Syntheses of the Carbamate Derivatives of 2 (5a-d).
Allyl(4-(4-(methoxymethoxy)phenoxy)phenyl)sulfane (10). A mixture of
compound 8 (6.5 g, 30 mmol), compound 9 (5.0 g, 30 mmol), as previously
synthesized,30 Cs2CO3 (15 g, 46 mmol), N,N-dimethylglycine hydrochloride
salt (1.3 g, 9.0 mmol), and CuI (0.85 g, 4.5 mmol) in dry 1,4-dioxane
(100 mL) was heated at 110 °C for 24 h. The mixture was diluted with
water and extracted with EtOAc. The combined organic layer was washed
with water and brine, dried over anhydrous Na2SO4, filtered, and
concentrated under reduced pressure. The crude product was purified by
silica gel chromatography. Compound 10 in 83% yield (7.5 g). 1H NMR (500
MHz, CDCl3) δ 3.48 (d, J = 6.98 Hz, 2 H), 3.51 (s, 3 H), 5.02-5.10 (m, 2
H), 5.16 (s, 2 H), 5.81-5.93 (m, J = 16.92, 9.99, 6.98, 6.98 Hz, 1 H),
6.87-6.92 (m, 2 H), 6.95-7.00 (m, 2 H), 7.02-7.08 (m, 2 H), 7.32-7.36 (m,
2 H). 13C NMR (126 MHz, CDCl3) δ 38.8, 56.1, 95.0, 117.6, 117.7, 118.3,
120.8, 128.6, 133.2, 134.0, 151.0, 153.7, 157.6. HRMS-ESI (m/z): [M+ H]+
calcd for C17H19O3S, 303.1079; found, 303.1053.
