$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Step 1. A mixture of aryl fluoride (55 a-d)
(2.0 mmol), 5-chloro-2-methoxyphenol (54 a) (0.32 g, 2.0 mmol) or
4-chloro-2-methoxyphenol (54 b) (0.32 g, 2.0 mmol) in DMSO (3.0 mL) and
anhydrous K2CO3 (0.41 g, 3.0 mmol) was heated at 120°C for 5 h. The
mixture was poured into ice water and extracted with EtOAc (3 × 50 mL).
The organic layer was sequentially washed with brine (2 × 75 mL), dried
over anhydrous Na2SO4, and concentrated in vacuo. The residue was
purified by column chromatography.
3-chloro-2-(5-chloro-2-methoxyphenoxy)benzonitrile (56 b): (0.48 g, 83%).
1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.65 (dd, J= 1.53, 7.96, 2H), 7.28 (dd, J=
4.99, 12.99 Hz, 1H), 7.13 - 6.81 (m, 2H), 6.54 (d, J = 2.42 Hz, 1H), 3.80
(s, 3H). 13C NMR (126 MHz, CDCl3) δ 153.09, 148.35, 146.28, 135.61,
132.44, 128.77, 126.25, 125.45, 124.06, 116.27, 114.31, 113.80, 109.04,
56.57.
