$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Table 2: A mixture of 2
mmol of aryl iodide, 3 mmol of phenol, 4 mmol of Cs2CO3, 0.04 mmol of
copper catalyst, 0.15 mmol of N,N-dimethylglycine hydrochlroide salt (or
0.2 mmols of CuI and 0.6 mmols of N,N-dimethylglycine hydrochlroide salt
in some cases), and 4 mL of dioxane in a sealed tube was heated at 90 °C
under nitrogen atmosphere. After the reaction completed monitored by TLC,
the cooled mixture was partitioned between ethyl acetate and water. The
organic layer was separated, and the aqueous layer was extracted with
ethyl acetate. The combined organic layers were washed with brine,dried
over Na2SO4, and concentrated in vacuo. The residual oil was loaded on a
silica gel column and eluted with ethyl acetate/petroleum ether (1/30) to
afford the product. 1-(4-tert-Butylphenoxy)-3-fluorobenzene 12, yield
83%. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz) δ 1.35 (s, 9H), 6.80 (m, 3H), 6.98 (m, 2H),
7.28 (m, 1H), 7.38 (m, 2H); MS m/z 244 (M+), 229, 201, 118, 117, 100, 91,
77, 65, 51; Anal. Calcd. for C16H17FO requires C: 78.66, H: 7.01, found
C: 78.81, H: 7.17.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM N,N-Dimethyl Glycine-Promoted Ullmann Coupling Reaction of Phenols and
Aryl Halides
