$DATUM Bis(4-(4-nitrophenoxy)phenyl)methylphenylsilane (7) A mixture of 1.00 g
(3.3 mmol) of 6, 0.95 g (6.9 mmol) of anhydrous K2CO3, 0.97 g (6.9 mmol)
of 1-fluoro-4-nitrobenzene and DMF (5.0 mL) was placed into a 50 mL flask
equipped with magnetic stirrer and condenser. The mixture was heated at
85 °C for 24 h. On cooling, the mixture was poured into 600 mL of an
ethanol–water solution (1:1 vol/vol) and a yellow solid was collected by
filtration. This product was washed with hot ethanol and then with water
and dried under vacuum at room temperature for 12 h.
Bis(4-(4-nitrophenoxy)phenyl)methylphenylsilane (7), yellow solid, Yield:
83 %. M.p.: 168–170 °C. IR (KBr, cm-1): 3024 (C–H arom.); 2952 (C–H
aliph.); 1597, 1579 (C=C arom.); 1509, 1339 (NO2); 1389, 1110 (Si–Ph);
1248 (C–O–C); 877 (arom. p-sust.); 790 (arom. mono-sust.). 1H NMR (CDCl3)
(δ) (ppm): 0.88 (s, 3H, CH3); 7.06 (d, J = 9.20 Hz, 4H(3)); 7.10 (d, J =
8.42 Hz,4H(6)); 7.36–7.55 (m, 5H, arom.); 7.57 (d, J = 8.43 Hz, 4H(2));
8.22 (d, J = 9.20 Hz, 4H(7)). 13C NMR (CDCl3) (δ) (ppm): -3.2 (CH3);
113.0 (C3); 117.5 (C1); 117.6 (C6); 119.8 (C7); 126.0 (C11); 128.1 (C12);
129.8 (C9); 132.7 (C8); 135.2 (C2); 137.3 (C10); 156.2 (C4); 162.8 (C5).
29Si NMR (CDCl3) (δ) (ppm): -11.0. Elem. Anal. Calcd. for C31H24N2O6Si;
(548.42): C: 67.89 %; H: 4.38 %; N: 5.11 %. Found: C: 67.21 %; H: 4.05 %;
N: 5.01 %.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis and characterization of new poly(amide)s derived from
bis(4-(4-aminophenoxy)phenyl)methylphenylsilane and
