$DATUM 3-[4-(4-Fluorophenoxy)phenyl]-1H-pyrazole (2). A mixture of
4-fluoroacetophenone (20 g, 0.14 mol, 1.0 eq), 4-fluorophenol (17.8 g,
0.16 mmol, 1.1 eq), and potassium carbonate (18 g, 0.13 mol, 0.9 eq) in
DMA (N,N-dimethylacetamide, 80 mL) was heated at 150°C for 16 hours. The
mixture was cooled to room temperature, diluted with CHCl3 (200 mL) and
washed with 2 N aqueous sodium hydroxide solution (2 x 100 mL). The
organic layer was dried over sodium sulfate, filtered and evaporated
under reduced pressure to afford the crude product (30 g). This was dried
under vacuum (40°C / 1 mmHg) for 2 hours to remove the volatile
impurities (DMA and 4-fluoroacetophenone), resulting in a viscous brown
oil (27 .5g, 83%). 4-fluoroacetophenone, yield 27 .5g, 83%. 1H NMR
(CDCl3) δ 7.93 (d, J = 8.7 Hz, 2H), 7.09-7.04 (m, 4H), 6.96 (d, J = 8.4
Hz, 2H), 2.57 (s, 3H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
