$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of 4-aryloxy-2,6-dibromo-1-nitrobenzenes 5 (general procedure).
Phenol (2 mmol) and K2CO3(0.28 g, 2 mmol) was added to a solution of
2,6-dibromo-4-fluoro-1-nitroso benzene (4) (0.56 g, 2 mmol) in DMSO (7
mL). The mixture was stirred at 40-50 °C for 30-40 min. The resulting
solution was cooled in an ice bath. The precipitate was filtered, washed
with water, and dried. 2,6-Dibromo-4-(4-methylphenoxy)-nitrosobenzene
(5a). Yield 0.61 g (83%). M.p. 113-115 °C (EtOH). Found (%): C, 42.34; H,
2.29; N, 3.60. C13H9NO2Br2. Calculated (%): C, 42.04; H, 2.42; N, 3.77.
1H NMR (CDCl3), δ: 2.40 (s, 3 H, Me); 6.99 (d, 2 H, H(2´), H(6´), J = 8.5
Hz); 7.24 (s, 2 H, H(3), H(5)); 7.25 (d, 2 H, H(3´), H(5´), J = 8.5 Hz).
HRMS: m/z 368.8995 [M]+. C13H9NO2Br2, calculated: M = 368.8992. MS, m/z
(I rel(%)): 371 [M]+(100), 340 (14), 262 (16), 181 (31), 153 (90),
91(41), 65 (34).
