$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure To a solution of NaOH (2.0
equiv., 40 mg, 1.0 mmol) in distilled water (2.5 mL) was added
alcohol/phenol (1.0 equiv., 0.5 mmol) at rt and the mixture was stirred
for a few minutes. Diaryliodonium salt 1 (1.2 equiv., 0.6 mmol) was added
in one portion and the reaction was vigorously stirred at rt or in an oil
bath preheated to 50 or 60 °C for the time detailed in Tables S2-S4. The
reaction was cooled to rt and extracted 3 times with EtOAc, dried over
MgSO4 or Na2SO4, filtered and concentrated in vacuo. The crude material
was purified with flash chromatography (pentane or pentane/EtOAc). Ether
2-4. (Cinnamyloxy)benzene (2a).
2-(2,4-Dimethylphenoxy)-1,3,5-trimethylbenzene (4g). Isolated as light
yellow oil (98 mg, 82 %).
