$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the diaryl ether
preparation: Cesium carbonate (7.36g, 22.6 mmol) was added to the phenol
(ArOH, 22.6 mmol) in 19 mL NMP. The slurry was degassed and filled with
nitrogen 3 times. The aryl halide (ArX: X=Br, I) (11.3 mmol) and
2,2,6,6-tetramethylheptane-3,5-dione (1.1 mmol) were added followed by
copper (I) chloride (5.6 mmol). The reaction mixture was degassed and
filled with nitrogen 3 times and then warmed to 120 °C under nitrogen.
Reactions were monitored by HPLC and stopped when >98 % conversion (by
peak area) was obtained. The reaction mixture was cooled to room
temperature and diluted with 25 mL MTBE. The slurry was filtered and
filter cake was washed with 25 mL MTBE. An 1 mL sample of the combined
filtrates was diluted 100 fold for assay yield. Combined filtrates were
washed subsequently with 35 mL 2N HCl, 35 mL 0.6N HCl, 30 mL 2M NaOH, 30
mL 10% NaCl. The resulting organic layer was dried over MgSO4 and
concentrated. This crude product mixture was then purified by either
flash column chromatography or direct crystallization as indicated. In
the case of flash column chromatographic purification, about 1 g crude
product was purified using about 100g silica gel 60 ( 230-400 mesh ASTM).
The number after each compound heading corresponds to the entry number in
Table 1. 4-(4-Fluorophenoxy)benzonitrile (2): It was prepared from
4-bromobenzonitrile and 4-fluorophenol in 90% assay yield after 90 min
age. About 1g portion of crude orange oil was purified by flash
chromatography (gradient hexanes/acetone, 400 mL each 99/1, 98/2, 97/3,
96/4) to give a white solid in 99% pure and 81% isolated yield, mp:
66-69°C. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400MHz) δ 7.62-7.60 (m, 2H), 7.14-7.03 (m, 4H),
7.00-6.97 (m, 2H); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 100 MHz) δ 161.9, 161.5 (d, J =
244Hz), 150. GC-MS m/z 213 (M+). (Lit ref 5b).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Ullmann Diaryl Ether Synthesis: Rate Acceleration by
2,2,6,6-Tetramethylheptane-3,5-dione
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
