$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of 2,3-bis[4-(4-nitrophenoxy)phenyl]quinoxaline (NPQ). Into a
100 mL round bottom flask equipped with a magnetic stirrer and a reflux
condenser, (HPQ) (6.908 g, 0.022 mol), p-chloronitrobenzene (7.126 g,
0.045 mol) and anhydrous K2CO3 (6.160 g, 0.045 mol) in DMF (26.4 mL) were
refluxed at 150°C for 8 h. The mixture was cooled to room temperature and
poured into methanol (200 mL) to precipitate a yellow solid which was
collected by filtration, washed with hot water, and dried. NPQ was
purified by recrystallization from DMF/CH3OH mixture. yellow solid,
Yield: 10.05 g (82%), Yield: 8.29 g (67%). MP.: 240°C. 1H NMR (CDCl3
ppm): 8.24-7.13, 7.64-7.09 and 8.19, 7.56. 13C NMR (CDCl3, ppm): 162.52,
155.54, 152.04, 142.90, 141.10, 135.80, 131.03, 130.37, 129.12, 125.02,
120.14 and 117.54.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Polyamides containing quinoxaline moiety
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Patil, Vidyadhar B.; Sayyed, Maheboob M.; Mahanwar, Prakash A.;
Wadgaonkar, Prakash P.; Maldar, Noormahmad N.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Polymer Research (2011), 18(4), 549-557

