$DATUM 1310-58-3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 1.2.1 Synthesis of halogenated nitro catechol
diphenyl ether 1a-1f 0.0110 mol halogenated hydroxydiphenyl ether was
heated to fusion followed by the addition of 0.0105 mol KOH. The reaction
was conducted for 15 min. 0.0100 mol substituted nitro chlorobenzene was
added in portions, and the mixture was heated to 150-175 °C. The reaction
process was detected by TLC (developing agent : petroleum ether : toluene
= 1 : 1, V : V). After the reaction was complete, the reaction system was
cooled and washed with 80 °C 5 % NaOH solution (3 × 15 mL) and boiling
water three times. The hot mixture was poured into cold water. The
solution was cooled, filtered and dried to afford the crude product as a
yellow granule, which was further recrystallized from anhydrous ethanol
to give product 1a-1f as a yellowish crystal. 1e, 81.5 %, yellowish
crystal m.p. 112-114 ℃; 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz) δ: 6.89 (d, J = 8.8 Hz,
1H, ArH), 7.13 (s, 1H, ArH), 7.00 (s, 1H, ArH), 7.23 (dd, J = 8.8, 2.4
Hz, 1H, ArH), 7.34 (dd, J = 8.6, 2.4 Hz, 2H, ArH), 7.42 (d, J = 2.4 Hz,
1H, ArH), 8.22 (dd, J = 8.6, 2.2 Hz, 2H, ArH); IR (KBr) ν: 3082 (Ar),
2361 (ArOAr), 1111 (ArCl), 1057 (ArBr) cm-1; MS m/z (%): 489 (M+, 100),
173 (37). Anal. cacld for C18H9BrCl3NO4: C 44.16, H 1.85, N 2.88; found C
44.19, H 1.86 N 2.86.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Studies on the synthesis and bactericidal activities of catechol diphenyl
ethers
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Ma, Meng-Lin; Xin, Ying; Wang, Yu-Liang; Gou, Shao-Hua; Chen, Shu-Hua
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Youji Huaxue (2004), 24(8), 927-932

$RFMT $RIREG SCHEME294 STEP1
$RXN



