$DATUM 109-99-9
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the reaction of
4-n-alkylphenoxides with pentafluorobenzene. 60% (w/w) sodium hydride in
mineral oil (1.1 equiv.) was charged to a round-bottomed flask (100 ml)
equipped with a magnetic follower. The reaction vessel evacuated under
high vacuum and back-filled with argon three times to create an inert
atmosphere. The sodium hydride was washed with dry hexane (10 ml), which
was removed using a syringe, and replaced with dry THF (40 ml). The
4-n-alkylphenol (1.0 equiv.) was dissolved in dry THF (10 ml), under an
atmosphere of argon, and carefully added to the sodium hydride mixture,
with stirring, to produce sodium 4-n-alkylphenoxide and hydrogen gas.
When the evolution of hydrogen gas had stopped pentafluorobenzene (1.0
equiv.) was added to the microwave vial and the reaction was heated to
reflux for 48 hr, left to cool, poured on to water (30 ml) and extracted
with dichloromethane (3 × 30 ml). The combined extracts were washed with
water (50 ml) and dried (MgSO4). The mixture was filtered and the solvent
removed in vacuo and purified by column chromatography on silica gel
using hexane as the eluent. 3-(4-Ethylphenoxy)-1,2,4,5-tetrafluorobenzene
(10) Reaction of 60% (w/w) sodium hydride in mineral oil (0.360 g, 9.00
mmol), 4-ethylphenol (1.000 g, 8.19 mmol) and pentafluorobenzene (1.376
g, 8.19 mmol). 1,2,4,5-Tetrafluoro-3-[4-n-heptyl]phenoxybenzene (12)
Reaction of 60% (w/w) sodium hydride in mineral oil (0.257 g, 6.41 mmol),
4-n-heptylphenol (1.002 g, 5.21 mmol) and pentafluorobenzene (0.965 g,
5.74 mmol). 1,2,4,5-tetrafluoro-3-[4-n-heptyl]phenoxybenzene 12 (1.126 g,
82 %) as a colourless oil. (Found: C, 67.20; H, 5.97. C19H20F4O requires
C, 67.05; H, 5.92 %); 1H NMR (500 MHz; CDCl3): δ 0.91 (3H, t, 3 J HH 7.0,
CH 3), 1.33 (8H, m, 4 × CH 2), 1.61 (2H, tm, 3 J HH = 7.0, (C'-4)-CH2-CH
2), 2.60 (2H, t, 3 J HH = 7.0, (C'-4)-CH 2), 6.91 (2H, dm, 3 J HH 8.5,
3'-H), 6.96 (1H, tt, 3 J HF 10.3, 4 J HF 7.0, 6-H), 7.16 (2H, dm, 3 J HH
8.5, 2'-H); 13C NMR (126 MHz; CDCl3): δ 14.30 (s, CH3), 22.91, (s, CH3
CH2), 29.41 (s, CH3(CH2)3 CH2), 29.41 (s, CH3(CH2)2 CH2), 31.81 (s,
CH3(CH2)4 CH2), 32.06 (s, CH3CH2 CH2), 35.37 (s, (4'-C)-CH2), 101.86 (t,
2 J CF 23.0, 6-C), 115.61 (s, 2'-C), 129.79 (s, 3'-C), 134.89 (tt, 2 J CF
12.6, 3 J CF 3.8, 3-C), 138.68 (s, 4'-C), 141.85 (dddd, 1 J CF 251, 2 J
CF 14.5, 3 J CF 5.0, 4 J CF 2.5, Ar-C), 146.68 (dddd, 1 J CF 248, 2 J CF
12.2, 3 J CF 12.2, 4 J CF 4.2, Ar-C), 155.52 (s, 1'-C); 19F NMR (658 MHz;
CDCl3; CFCl3): δ -139.46 (2F, ddd, 3 J FF = 21.6, 3 J FH = 10.0, 5 J FF =
10.3, 1-CF and 5-CF), -154.66 (2F, ddd, 3 J FF = 21.6, J FH = 7.0, 5 J FF
= 10.3, 2-CF and 4-CF); m/z (EI+) 340 (M+, 2%), 256 (8), 255 (100), 206
(12), 89 (22), 78 (25), 43 (67), 29 (40).
