$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for Synthesis of 3 Potassium carbonate (3 mmol), and
dihalide 2 (6 mmol), and DMF (1 mL) were added in this order to a
two-necked flask equipped with a reflux condenser at 15°C. A DMF solution
(4 mL) of (S)-binaphthol (1.1 mmol) was added to this solution over 1 h.
After addition, the mixture was stirred 8 h under reflux. The reaction
mixture was quenched by pouring it into water. The precipitate was
collected by suction filtration, washed with water, and dried under
reduced pressure. The solid was purified by silica-gel column
chromatography (CHCl3/hexane = 2:1) to afford the corresponding dihalide
3. 3a, yield 82% [φ]25D: -86; 1H NMR δ (300 MHz, CDCl3): 6.82 (4H, d, J =
9.0 Hz), 7.09 (4H, t, J = 8.4 Hz), 7.29-7.31 (6H, m), 7.43 (2H, t, J =
5.7 Hz), 7.54 (4H, d, J= 9.0 Hz), 7.68 (4H, dd, J = 5.1. 8.4 Hz), 7.90
(2H, d, J = 9.0 Hz), 7.95 (2H, d, J = 8.7 Hz) ppm.
