$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 7-chloro-1-fluoro-9-hydroxydibenzo[b, f][1,4]oxazepin-11(10H)-one (43)
Following the general procedure II,
N-(4-chloro-2,6-dihydroxyphenyl)-2,6-difluorobenzamide (30.0 mg, 0.1
mmol), NaOH (16 mg, 0.4 mmol) and 1.5 ml DMF were used. The reaction
mixture was stirred at 100 °C for 2h. After completion of the reaction,
the residue was purified by silical gel column chromatography (petroleum
ether: ethyl acetate = 1:1). Finally, compound (43) was isolated. (23 mg,
yellow solid), 82% yield. 1H-NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ (ppm) 10.7 (s, 1H),
9.9 (s, 1H), 7.62-7.56 (m, 1H), 7.25-7.12 (m, 2H), 6.97 (d, J = 1.2 Hz,
1H), 6.76 (s, 1H); 13C-NMR (100 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ (ppm) 166.9, 162.0,
161.4, 161.3, 160.2, 160.1, 159.4, 153.6, 150.6, 133.9, 133.8, 131.6,
131.4, 128.8, 128.6, 118.2, 116.6, 116.5, 115.5, 115.4, 113.9, 113.7,
112.8, 111.8, 111.6; LRMS (ESI) calcd for C13H8ClFNO3 [M+H]+: 280.01
found 279.98
