$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 4-(3-Nitrophenoxy)phenylamine Hydrochloride (27). To a 100 mL
round-bottomed flask equipped with a magnetic stirring bar were added
4-acetamidophenol (3.3 g, 22 mmol), 1-fluoro-3-nitrobenzene (2.8 g, 20
mmol), K2CO3 (3.0 g, 22 mmol), and DMF (40 mL). The reaction mixture was
heated at 150 °C for 15 h under N2. After cooling to room temperature,
the reaction mixture was poured into 500 mL of ice-cold water and stirred
for 0.5 h. The precipitate formed was collected by filtration, washed
with water, and dried in a vacuum oven overnight to yield
N-(4-(3-nitrophenoxy)phenyl)acetamide (4.8 g, 18 mmol, 82%) as a yellow
solid. N-(4-(3-nitrophenoxy)phenyl)acetamide, yield (4.8 g, 82%) 1H NMR
(CDCl3; 400 MHz): δ 2.21 (s, 3), 7.03-7.06 (m, 2H), 7.22-7.56 (m, 4H),
7.75-7.77 (m, 1H), 7.91-7.93 (m, 1H). MS (ESI, pos. ion) m/z: 273 (M +
1); (ESI, neg. ion) 271 (M - 1).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM first stage thermal
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
