$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (4-(4-tert-Butylphenoxy)phenyl)(methyl)sulfide, Figure 7. A Flame dried
microwave vial equipped with a stir bar under a blanket of argon was
charged with Cu-Ni/C (100 mg, 8 mol % Cu), Cs2CO3 (651 mg, 1.2 equiv),
1,10-phenanthroline (90 mg, 0.5 equiv), 4-bromothianisole (203 mg, 1
equiv), 4-tert-butylphenol (300 mg, 2 equiv) and dioxane (2.5 mL). The
mixture was vigorously stirred before it was placed in the microwave
reactor and heated to 200 °C for 60 min. Upon cooling, the reaction
mixture was filtered through celite, solvents removed and the column
chromatography with 8% EtOAc in hexanes yielded product as a white solid
in 81% yield (314 mg). The spectral data matched those previously
reported for this compound.10
(4-(4-tert-Butylphenoxy)phenyl)(methyl)sulfide, yield (314 mg, 81%).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
